Article 2 The International Commercial Court shall accept the following cases:
(1) first-instance international commercial cases in which the parties have by agreement chosen the jurisdiction of the Supreme People's Court in accordance with Article 277 of the Civil Procedure Law and the subject matter amount is RMB 300 million yuan or more;
(2) first-instance international commercial cases under the jurisdiction of a Higher People's Court which the Higher People's Court considers need to be tried by the Supreme People's Court and has obtained approval for;
(3) first-instance international commercial cases of major national impact;
(4) applications for arbitration preservation, applications for setting aside or enforcement of international commercial arbitration awards in accordance with Article 14 of these Provisions;
(5) other international commercial cases which the Supreme People's Court considers shall be tried by the International Commercial Court.

Article 3 Commercial cases with any of the following circumstances may be determined as international commercial cases as referred to in these Provisions:
(1) one or both parties are foreigners, stateless persons, foreign enterprises or organizations;
(2) the habitual residence of one or both parties is outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(3) the subject matter is located outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(4) the legal facts that give rise to, alter or extinguish commercial relations occur outside the territory of the People's Republic of China.

Article 8 When the International Commercial Court, in trying a case, shall apply foreign law, it may ascertain the foreign law through the following means:
(1) provided by the parties;
(2) provided by the central authorities or competent authorities of the other country through judicial assistance channels;
(3) provided by the Chinese embassy or consulate in that country or the embassy or consulate of that country in China upon request by the Supreme People's Court;
(4) provided by participants in the legal ascertainment cooperation mechanism established or joined by the Supreme People's Court;
(5) provided by experts of the International Commercial Expert Committee of the Supreme People's Court;
(6) provided by legal ascertainment service institutions or Chinese and foreign legal experts;
(7) other appropriate means.
The foreign legal materials and expert opinions provided through the above means shall be presented in court in accordance with the provisions of law, and the opinions of all parties shall be fully heard.
